                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "dynamic, arcade-style action game in which the player fights waves of giant insects, developing their character and surviving increasingly difficult encounters.\n\n✅wide variety of insects with unique traits.\n✅Dynamic, intense battles against waves of enemies.\n✅Good graphics and good sound.\n✅Progression system (leveling and upgrades).\n✅A diverse arsenal of weapons (classic and fantasy).\n✅The price is good.\n\n❌The game is not suitable for long-term play because the gameplay pattern is repetitive: running, shooting, surviving a wave, upgrading the next wave.\n❌Multiplayer mode, but there are no people.\n❌The maps are barely different.\n\n\n✅✅ Verdict: [strike] Terrible [/strike] , [strike] Bad [/strike] , [strike] Mediocre [/strike] , [b] Decent [/b] , [strike] Good [/strike] , [strike] Very Good [/strike] (Rating scale for short games, retro indie simulator games and similar)\n\n[quote] If you'd like to see more of my reviews, you can find them on my\ncurator page:\n[url=https://store.steampowered.com/curator/45994324/admin/reviews_manage/]CuratorKingViking[/url]\nand on my group:\n[url=https://steamcommunity.com/groups/CuratorKingViking]GroupKingViking[/url]\n\nIf you have any questions about my reviews, feel free to ask.\nI’m happy to answer them. All reviews are my own!!\nBest regards, King Viking Bezimienny, Polish Game Reviewer. [/quote]",
